    },
    {
      "text": "\n###Pivot\n\n>Pivots make it possible for you to convert a row into a column. \n>transpose a dataset from rows to columns and columns to rows. Pivot is one of the techniques that allows transposing of rows to columns and performs possible aggregations along the way",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "ca2780531ddf424a8cf89"
    },
    {
      "text": "####Variance and Standard Deviation\n  These are both measures of the spread of the data around the mean. \n#### skewness and kurtosis\nThe skewness is a measure of symmetry or asymmetry of data distribution,\n and kurtosis measures whether data is heavy-tailed or light-tailed in a distribution\n\n#### Covariance and Correlation\nTwo of these functions are cov and corr, for\ncovariance and correlation, respectively. Correlation measures the Pearson correlation\ncoefficient, which is scaled between –1 and +1. The covariance is scaled according to the inputs\nin the data.\n\n[DataSkewness](https://community.cloud.databricks.com/?o=2941430867364584#notebook/2227913417139108/command/2227913417139127)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "2a18671f5bc34178a1c55"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n//retailDF.select(f.collect_set(f.col(\"Country\")).as(\"setOfCountry\"), f.collect_list(f.col(\"Country\")).as(\"listOfCountry\"))\n\nretailDF.agg(f.collect_set(f.col(\"Country\")).as(\"setOfCountry\"), f.collect_list(f.col(\"Country\")).as(\"listOfCountry\"))\n.withColumn(\"countryOne\",col(\"setOfCountry\")(0))\n.show()\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
