    {
      "text": "#### LAG ve LEAD\n\nIt can be helpful to compare rows with previous or next rows, especially if you have the data in a meaningful order. You can use LAG or LEAD to create columns that pull values from other rows; All you have to do is specify which column you want to pull from and how many rows away you want to pull from. LAG pulls from the top rows, LEAD from the bottom rows.\n\nNow let’s see how different the salary differs from the previous and next employee in order of id (probably entry order).",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
