    },
    {
      "text": "###Count\n1. when\nperforming a count(*), Spark will count null values (including rows containing all nulls). However,\nwhen counting an individual column, Spark will not count the null values.\n\n2. counting on column is a transformation not a action like df.count()\n\n      - count(*) : count on all column\n      - count(1) : count all row as literal 1\n\n```\ndf.select(f.count(\"*\"), f.count(\"description\")).show()\n+--------+------------------+\n|count(1)|count(description)|\n+--------+------------------+\n|   19632|             19563|\n+--------+------------------+\n```",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
